        "facts": ["Sundiata defeated Soumaoro Kanté of Sosso at Kirina around 1235.", "He became the first ruler of the Mali Empire.", "The epic is told among the Mande peoples."],
        "misconceptions": ["The Epic of Sundiata is pure fantasy with no connection to real history."] },
      { "key": "hero-pattern", "title": "Explain the epic's heroic pattern", "description": "Identifies prophecy, early weakness, exile and return in Sundiata's story.",
        "concept": "Heroic pattern", "definition": "Many epics follow a pattern of prophecy, humble or hard beginnings, exile and a triumphant return; Sundiata's story follows it.",
        "facts": ["A prophecy foretells his greatness.", "He cannot walk as a child and is mocked.", "He is driven into exile and returns to free his people."],
        "misconceptions": ["Sundiata is a hero from birth with no hardship to overcome."] },
      { "key": "griots", "title": "Explain the role of the griot", "description": "Describes what griots do and how they preserve and transmit the epic.",
        "concept": "Griots (jeli)", "definition": "Griots are hereditary West African bards, historians and genealogists who preserve and perform the history of peoples and families.",
        "facts": ["Griots are called jeli in Mande languages.", "The role is hereditary within griot families.", "They recite history and genealogies, often with the kora or balafon.", "Griots also served as advisers to rulers."],
        "misconceptions": ["Griots are simply entertainers with no role as historians."] },
      { "key": "orality", "title": "Explain how oral literature differs from written texts", "description": "Explains variation between performances and the absence of a single authoritative text.",
        "concept": "Oral literature", "definition": "Oral literature lives in performance, so it exists in many versions adapted to audience and occasion rather than in one fixed text.",
        "facts": ["Each performance adapts to its audience and occasion.", "Different griots and regions tell the epic differently.", "Written versions record particular tellings, not the one true text."],
        "misconceptions": ["The written translation is the original, correct version of the epic.", "Oral literature is less sophisticated than written literature."] }
    ],
    "translations": {
      "ko": { "title": "순디아타 서사시와 그리오 전통",
        "instructions": "시험관이 순디아타 서사시에 대해 이야기합니다. 이 서사시가 무엇을 이야기하는지, 누가 그것을 이어 가는지, 구전 문학이 기록된 텍스트와 어떻게 다른지 자신의 말로 설명하세요. 모르면 \"모르겠습니다\"라고 말하세요.",
        "objectives": { "story": "이야기와 그 역사적 배경 요약하기", "hero-pattern": "서사시의 영웅 서사 유형 설명하기", "griots": "그리오의 역할 설명하기", "orality": "구전 문학과 기록된 텍스트의 차이 설명하기" } },
